; UDON-THEORY-canon — provisional canonical outline
;
; Conventions: FORMAT.md. Identity lives in the slug; ordering lives here.
;
; 2026-07-31: project-frame chapter and secondary-carried "AAT results" removed.
; Those files were a sterilized paste of TST vocabulary (P* as "advantages,"
; document scorecards, manufacture slogans) without identification structure,
; primary derivation, or first-principles chain. Not demoted — deleted.
; What remains is corpus process (arrangement) plus one demand-ranking
; observation. Theory foundation for UDON is a bare gap until rebuilt from
; AAT/TST primaries properly — not from plain-language compression of P1–P6.
;
; Row shapes: |segment[slug]… | gap (bare) | arc
; Reordering costs nothing. Renaming a slug costs everything downstream.

|outline[udon-theory-canon] :version 0.2-provisional :date 2026-07-31
  :governed-by FORMAT.md
  :segments-dir src/
  :purpose Claims that resolve (or honestly bound) paths, schemas, dialects, value typing, and tooling — once they have a real foundation
  :note Part I is not a foundation story yet. Arrangement norms are process. Demand ranking is evidence about a report. The theory root is open.

  ; ===========================================================================
  |part[why] :n I
    :title What is standing (and what is not)
    |arc
      Only two kinds of content are present: (1) how *this* claim corpus is written
      under agent turnover — process, not UDON theory; (2) what the demand report
      ranks as customer. Everything that pretended to be a TST/AAT-rooted project
      frame was removed. Do not re-add P*-slogan layers or scorecard tables without
      a derivation that would survive ASF audit.

    ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    |chapter[arrangement] :title "Outline + segments — process for this corpus"
      |arc
        Corpus-authoring discipline. Not a substitute for domain theory.

      |segment[intro-udon-theory].discussion :status discussion-grade :stage draft :max discussion-grade
        Orientation only — no warrant
      |segment[form-present-truth-collision].formulation :status heuristic :stage draft :max robust-qualitative
        Present-truth can collide; append-only history need not
      |segment[norm-gap-as-discontinuity].normative :status decided :stage draft :max decided
        Bare gaps mark broken links; no id, no predicted fill
      |segment[form-identity-ordering-split].formulation :status heuristic :stage draft :max robust-qualitative
        Slug = identity; outline = order
      |segment[norm-proxy-discipline].normative :status decided :stage draft :max decided
        Proxies locate; they do not settle

    ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    |chapter[demand-anchor] :title "Demand ranking (not theory)"
      |arc
        One observation about the demand evidence base. Does not found paths, schema,
        or dialects. Does not replace a first-principles root.

      |segment[obs-mutation-customer].observation :status robust-qualitative :stage draft :max robust-qualitative
        Demand report ranks schema-guarded structural mutation first; paths/schema/spans are its inputs

    ; -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    |gap
      Precedes: corpus process norms and a demand ranking.
      Follows: (nothing — no theory root yet).
      Missing: a foundation that would connect agent/document work to AAT identification
      structure (observation channels, intervention, tempo, persistence) the way ASF does —
      with named premises, consequences, and transfer conditions — not a list of "advantages"
      and not a scorecard of documents vs software slogans. Rebuild only from primaries under
      ~/src/arch/asf/, or from original derivation here; do not reconstitute the deleted P* layer.
